From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dinesh Choudhary <idinesh@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 10:51:47 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 18/19] fix(qti): notify SAIL on vendor warm reset too

Downstream TZ's tzbsp_psci_status_com() maps PSCI_WARM_RESET_CMD to its
own SAIL message, MD_SOC_WR (0xB2200320), distinct from hard reset's
MD_SOC_HR. qti_system_reset2() only notified SAIL for the hard-reset
vendor sub-type, leaving the companion die unaware of a warm reset.

Add qti_sail_comm_system_warm_reset() alongside the existing
qti_sail_comm_system_reset()/qti_sail_comm_system_off() and call it for
the warm-reset sub-type, mirroring hard reset's existing notify-then-
wait-for-ack handling.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-sonnet-5
Signed-off-by: Dinesh Choudhary <idinesh@qti.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/qualcomm-linux/trusted-firmware-a/pull/135]
Signed-off-by: Roshan Sivakumar <roshs@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 drivers/qti/sail_comm/sail_comm.c         |  6 ++++++
 include/drivers/qti/sail_comm/sail_comm.h |  2 ++
 plat/qti/common/src/qti_pm.c              | 10 ++++++----
 3 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/qti/sail_comm/sail_comm.c b/drivers/qti/sail_comm/sail_comm.c
index d7f50aafa..8e3659ede 100644
--- a/drivers/qti/sail_comm/sail_comm.c
+++ b/drivers/qti/sail_comm/sail_comm.c
@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@
 
 #define QTI_SAIL_RESET_READY		U(0xA0300100)
 #define QTI_MD_GRACEFUL_SHUTDOWN	U(0xB2200430)
+#define QTI_MD_SOC_WR			U(0xB2200320)
 #define QTI_MD_SOC_HR			U(0xB2200510)
 #define QTI_MD_SD_TZ_SRC		U(0xB2)
 #define QTI_MD_SD_NO_ACK		U(0x10)
@@ -88,6 +89,11 @@ void qti_sail_comm_system_reset(void)
 	qti_md_sd_psci_status_com(QTI_MD_SOC_HR);
 }
 
+void qti_sail_comm_system_warm_reset(void)
+{
+	qti_md_sd_psci_status_com(QTI_MD_SOC_WR);
+}
+
 void qti_sail_comm_system_off(void)
 {
 	qti_md_sd_psci_status_com(QTI_MD_GRACEFUL_SHUTDOWN);
diff --git a/include/drivers/qti/sail_comm/sail_comm.h b/include/drivers/qti/sail_comm/sail_comm.h
index 25e8ebb1b..9a5c12cbe 100644
--- a/include/drivers/qti/sail_comm/sail_comm.h
+++ b/include/drivers/qti/sail_comm/sail_comm.h
@@ -12,11 +12,13 @@
 /* Notify a companion SAIL die before the platform powers off or resets. */
 void qti_sail_comm_system_off(void);
 void qti_sail_comm_system_reset(void);
+void qti_sail_comm_system_warm_reset(void);
 
 #else
 
 static inline void qti_sail_comm_system_off(void) {}
 static inline void qti_sail_comm_system_reset(void) {}
+static inline void qti_sail_comm_system_warm_reset(void) {}
 
 #endif /* QTI_SAIL_COMM */
 
diff --git a/plat/qti/common/src/qti_pm.c b/plat/qti/common/src/qti_pm.c
index 1bec50ebc..d612c4be0 100644
--- a/plat/qti/common/src/qti_pm.c
+++ b/plat/qti/common/src/qti_pm.c
@@ -231,13 +231,15 @@ static int qti_system_reset2(int is_vendor, int reset_type, u_register_t cookie)
 	}
 
 	/*
-	 * A vendor hard reset is the same SoC-level reset as the
-	 * architectural SYSTEM_RESET, so it needs the same companion SAIL
-	 * die heads-up before PS_HOLD is deasserted. Warm reset has no
-	 * equivalent downstream SAIL notification, so it is left alone.
+	 * Both vendor reset sub-types need a companion SAIL die heads-up
+	 * before PS_HOLD is deasserted, same as the architectural
+	 * SYSTEM_RESET: hard reset mirrors qti_system_reset()'s notification,
+	 * while warm reset uses its own distinct SAIL message.
 	 */
 	if (((uint32_t)reset_type & QTI_RESET2_TYPE_MASK) == QTI_PON_CFG_HARD_RESET) {
 		qti_sail_comm_system_reset();
+	} else {
+		qti_sail_comm_system_warm_reset();
 	}
 
 	assert_ps_hold();
